# =============================================================================
# officeAI — local environment template
# Copy to .env and fill in values for local dev.
# =============================================================================

# Nothing is required at runtime today — the Next.js editor and the
# `office-agent` CLI both run with zero env. This file exists so that
# release-pipeline secrets that DO need attention (and live on GitHub,
# not on disk) are at least discoverable from the repo root.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release pipeline (GitHub Actions only — NOT used by `make dev`)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: .github/workflows/auto-release.yml (the `notify-hof-os` job).
# Used to push a `chore(officeai): bump to X.Y.Z` commit into
# `jhoetter/hof-os` on every successful office-ai release. Without it,
# auto-release.yml's first two jobs still succeed (build + GitHub
# Release) but hof-os won't pick up the new version automatically.
#
# This is a GitHub Actions secret — do NOT put it in a local .env file.
# The line below is for documentation only.
#
# Where to get it (one-time, ~3 min):
#   1. Open https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#      (Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens
#       → Fine-grained tokens → Generate new token)
#   2. Token name:           OFFICEAI_SYNC_TOKEN
#      Resource owner:       jhoetter
#      Expiration:           1 year (set a calendar reminder to renew)
#      Repository access:    Only select repositories → jhoetter/hof-os
#                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
#                            IMPORTANT: scope to hof-os, NOT office-ai.
#                            The secret LIVES in office-ai but the token
#                            AUTHENTICATES against hof-os (that's the
#                            repo we push the bump commit into).
#      Permissions →
#        Repository permissions:
#          • Contents:  Read and write
#          • Metadata:  Read-only   (auto-selected; cannot be turned off)
#   3. Click "Generate token", copy the `github_pat_…` string.
#   4. Open https://github.com/jhoetter/office-ai/settings/secrets/actions
#      → New repository secret
#      Name:   OFFICEAI_SYNC_TOKEN
#      Secret: <the token from step 3>
#
# Verify by triggering a push to office-ai/main and watching the
# `notify-hof-os` job in Actions: it should commit to hof-os/main
# without an auth error. Common gotcha: GitHub defaults the
# `Contents` permission to `Read-only` — flip it to `Read and write`,
# otherwise `Checkout hof-os` will succeed but `git push` will fail
# with exit code 128.
#
# OFFICEAI_SYNC_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
